# trend_g1.py output (DERIVED; every slope and ratio is computed, no vendor prints it)

Inputs: 389 LUT rows, 96 verified G1 rows; 363 printed wood points (grade a/b, not fallback) before the per-diameter dedupe.
Series with >= 2 diameters: 63 (LUT only 42, G1 only 21).

## A. Chipload against diameter, every series with >= 2 sizes (mm/tooth)
Frame = the diameter the series keys on. 'copy of' = the same printed cell as the named
material (a shared chart row); it is not a second witness.

